this_type leaks into codegen when [Differentiable] function returns an interface type (invalid HLSL, ICE on SPIRV)
## Issue Description

When a `[Differentiable]` function returns an interface (existential) type and a method is dispatched on the returned value, Slang fails to lower `this_type` before emit. On HLSL, this produces invalid output (a forward declaration with `this_type<Tuple_N>` parameter and a mismatched-arity call site). On SPIRV, it produces an internal compiler error.

## Reproducer Code

```hlsl
public struct SurfaceInteraction { public float3 pos; }
public struct MaterialProperties { public float3 albedo; }

public interface IMaterialInstance
{
    MaterialProperties collect_properties(SurfaceInteraction si);
}

struct MyInst : IMaterialInstance
{
    MaterialProperties collect_properties(SurfaceInteraction si)
    {
        MaterialProperties p;
        p.albedo = si.pos;
        return p;
    }
}

[Differentiable]
IMaterialInstance get_inst(SurfaceInteraction si)
{
    return MyInst();
}

RWStructuredBuffer<float3> out_buf;

[shader("compute")]
[numthreads(1,1,1)]
void main()
{
    SurfaceInteraction si;
    si.pos = float3(1, 2, 3);
    out_buf[0] = get_inst(si).collect_properties(si).albedo;
}
```

**Commands:**

```bash
slangc repro.slang -target hlsl  -entry main -stage compute -o repro.hlsl   # exit 0, invalid HLSL
slangc repro.slang -target spirv -entry main -stage compute -o repro.spv    # ICE
```

Removing `[Differentiable]` from `get_inst` makes both bugs disappear — Slang fully specializes the existential and emits clean code.

Reproduced on `slangc -v` → `2026.8.1-20-gf23b358b5`.

## Expected Behavior

Slang either specializes the dispatch away (as it does without `[Differentiable]`), or emits a valid dispatcher with consistent declaration and call-site arity. No `this_type<...>` should reach the backend.

## Actual Behavior

### `-target hlsl`: invalid output (slangc exits 0)

```hlsl
// Forward declaration — never defined, contains internal IR type name:
MaterialProperties_0 IMaterialInstance_collect_properties_0(this_type<Tuple_0 > _0, SurfaceInteraction_0 _1);

// Call site — passes only 1 argument despite the 2-parameter declaration:
MaterialProperties_0 _S1 = IMaterialInstance_collect_properties_0(si_0);
```

dxc rejects this with `unknown type name 'this_type'` and `expected ')'` at the call site.

### `-target spirv`: internal compiler error

```
error[E99997]: Slang compilation aborted due to an exception of N5Slang13InternalErrorE unimplemented: Unhandled global inst in spirv-emit:
let  %1	: _	= this_type(%Tuple)
```

## Test Plan

- [x] Add a regression test under `tests/autodiff/` covering the pattern above, asserting that emitted HLSL contains no `this_type` token and that SPIRV emission succeeds.
- [x] Existing autodiff tests under `tests/autodiff/` continue to pass.

